# RFC 1628 (UPS-MIB) fixture for driver-conformance testing of NUT's snmp-ups driver in
# `mibs=ietf` mode. Values were chosen to match, and have been verified against, NUT's real
# ietf-mib.c OID mapping table (upstream networkupstools/nut), not guessed: an Online UPS at
# 100% charge, 60 minutes (3600s) runtime, 10% load. Lines must stay in strict ascending OID
# order -- snmpsim serves GETNEXT/walk by file position, and out-of-order OIDs break SNMP walk
# semantics with an "OID not increasing" error partway through.
#
# Community: public (SNMPv1/SNMPv2c). This fixture intentionally covers community-based auth
# only; see images/snmpsim-fixture/README.md for the SNMPv3 coverage gap this leaves.
1.3.6.1.2.1.1.1.0|4|nut-operator simulated UPS
1.3.6.1.2.1.1.2.0|6|1.3.6.1.2.1.33
1.3.6.1.2.1.33.1.1.1.0|4|nut-operator
1.3.6.1.2.1.33.1.1.2.0|4|snmpsim-fixture
1.3.6.1.2.1.33.1.1.3.0|4|1.0
1.3.6.1.2.1.33.1.2.1.0|2|2
1.3.6.1.2.1.33.1.2.3.0|2|60
1.3.6.1.2.1.33.1.2.4.0|2|100
1.3.6.1.2.1.33.1.4.1.0|2|3
1.3.6.1.2.1.33.1.4.4.1.5.1|2|10
